Root cause:
The bug was caused by the Ambari Server not properly handling the state of the topology when the server was restarted after the creation of a cluster using a blueprint. Specifically, the system did not check if the topology was resolved for the cluster before attempting to start the topology task executor, which led to issues when scaling the cluster. The patch added a check to ensure that the topology is resolved before starting the executor, thus addressing the problem.
